  "tagline": "Greek late-1990s transactional SQL server with a built-in programmable web server; long defunct.",
  "description": "Ovrimos was a client/server relational database from Ovrimos S.A. of Athens, Greece (founded 1993, with a US office in Mountain View), whose distinguishing feature was a built-in, programmable web server so that SQL-backed web applications could be served straight from the database. Sold around 2000 as Ovrimos WebBase Server 3.x, it claimed ANSI SQL compliance, transactions, an ODBC driver, a replicator and secure web serving in higher editions, and a tiny footprint of about 4 MB of disk and 10 MB of RAM. The company also sold an S/MIME e-mail and LDAP product, and the database disappeared in the early 2000s. It is of interest today mainly as an early 'database plus application server' design.",
